## Vercel Speed Insights Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this Next.js 16 App Router project.

### Changes Made

**Modified:**
- `app/layout.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights component import and integration
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package dependencies

### Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart), I:

1. **Installed the package:** Used npm to install `@vercel/speed-insights` 
2. **Integrated the component:** Added the `SpeedInsights` component from `@vercel/speed-insights/next` to the root layout file (`app/layout.tsx`)
3. **Placed it correctly:** The component is rendered at the end of the `<body>` tag, following Next.js App Router best practices

The implementation follows the framework-specific instructions for Next.js 13.5+ with the App Router pattern. The SpeedInsights component will automatically track Core Web Vitals and performance metrics once the application is deployed to Vercel.

### Verification

- ✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
- ✅ Linting passed with no errors (`npm run lint`)
- ✅ All tests passed (15 passed, 10 skipped due to test environment requirements)
- ✅ TypeScript compilation successful
- ✅ Lock file updated correctly

### Notes

The Speed Insights tracking will be automatically activated when the application is deployed to Vercel. No additional configuration or API keys are required. Performance metrics will be available in the Vercel dashboard under "Speed Insights" after deployment and user visits.
